      "text": "Given the quadratic expression \\(x^2 + bx + 2008\\) factors into a product of two binomials with integer coefficients, we can write it as:\n\n\\[\n(x + p)(x + q) = x^2 + (p + q)x + pq\n\\]\n\nwhere \\(p\\) and \\(q\\) are integers. We know that:\n\n\\[\npq = 2008 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad p + q = b\n\\]\n\nTo find the smallest positive integer \\(b\\), we need to determine the factor pairs \\((p, q)\\) of 2008 and compute the corresponding \\(b = p + q\\). We should start with the factor pairs since smaller \\(|p - q|\\) might yield smaller \\(b\\).\n\nThe factor pairs of 2008 are:\n\\[\n(1, 2008), (-1, -2008), (2, 1004), (-2, -1004), (4, 502), (-4, -502), (8, 251), (-8, -251)\n\\]\n\nWe now calculate \\(b = p + q\\) for each pair:\n\\[\n\\begin{aligned}\n&\\text{For } p = 1 \\text{ and } q = 2008: & b &= 1 + 2008 = 2009 \\\\\n&\\text{For } p = -1 \\text{ and } q = -2008: & b &= -1 + (-2008) = -2009 \\\\\n&\\text{For } p = 2 \\text{ and } q = 1004: & b &= 2 + 1004 = 1006 \\\\\n&\\text{For } p = -2 \\text{ and } q = -1004: & b &= -2 + (-1004) = -1006 \\\\\n&\\text{For } p = 4 \\text{ and } q = 502: & b &= 4 + 502 = 506 \\\\\n&\\text{For } p = -4 \\text{ and } q = -502: & b &= -4 + (-502) = -506 \\\\\n&\\text{For } p = 8 \\text{ and } q = 251: & b &= 8 + 251 = 259 \\\\\n&\\text{For } p = -8 \\text{ and } q = -251: & b &= -8 + (-251) = -259 \\\\\n\\end{aligned}\n\\]\n\nAmong these, the smallest positive value of \\(b\\) is 259, which corresponds to the factor pair \\((8, 251)\\).\n\nThus, the smallest positive integer \\(b\\) for which \\(x^2 + bx + 2008\\) factors into a product of two binomials with integer coefficients is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{259}\n\\]",
