      "text": "To factor the quadratic expression \\(x^2 + bx + 2008\\) into a product of two binomials with integer coefficients, we need to express it in the form \\((x + p)(x + q)\\), where \\(p\\) and \\(q\\) are integers. This means that:\n\n\\[x^2 + bx + 2008 = (x + p)(x + q) = x^2 + (p + q)x + pq.\\]\n\nFrom this, we can see that the constant term \\(pq\\) must be equal to 2008, and the coefficient of \\(x\\) must be equal to \\(p + q\\). Therefore, we need to find pairs of integers \\((p, q)\\) such that \\(pq = 2008\\) and then determine which pair, along with the appropriate value of \\(b\\), satisfies \\(p + q = -b\\).\n\nFirst, let's find the factor pairs of 2008. The prime factorization of 2008 is:\n\n\\[2008 = 2^3 \\times 251.\\]\n\nThe factor pairs of 2008 are:\n\\[\n(1, 2008), (-1, -2008), (2, 1004), (-2, -1004), (4, 502), (-4, -502), (8, 251), (-8, -251).\n\\]\n\nFor each pair \\((p, q)\\), the value of \\(b\\) is \\(-(p + q)\\). We will calculate \\(b\\) for each pair:\n\n1. For \\((p, q) = (1, 2008)\\):\n   \\[p + q = 1 + 2008 = 2009 \\Rightarrow b = -2009.\\]\n\n2. For \\((p, q) = (-1, -2008)\\):\n   \\[p + q = -1 - 2008 = -2009 \\Rightarrow b = 2009.\\]\n\n3. For \\((p, q) = (2, 1004)\\):\n   \\[p + q = 2 + 1004 = 1006 \\Rightarrow b = -1006.\\]\n\n4. For \\((p, q) = (-2, -1004)\\):\n   \\[p + q = -2 - 1004 = -1006 \\Rightarrow b = 1006.\\]\n\n5. For \\((p, q) = (4, 502)\\):\n   \\[p + q = 4 + 502 = 506 \\Rightarrow b = -506.\\]\n\n6. For \\((p, q) = (-4, -502)\\):\n   \\[p + q = -4 - 502 = -506 \\Rightarrow b = 506.\\]\n\n7. For \\((p, q) = (8, 251)\\):\n   \\[p + q = 8 + 251 = 259 \\Rightarrow b = -259.\\]\n\n8. For \\((p, q) = (-8, -251)\\):\n   \\[p + q = -8 - 251 = -259 \\Rightarrow b = 259.\\]\n\nAmong all these values, the smallest positive integer value for \\(b\\) is 2. Therefore, the smallest positive integer \\(b\\) for which \\(x^2 + bx + 2008\\) factors into a product of two binomials, each having integer coefficients, is:\n\n\\(\\boxed{2}\\)",
